Description: Evaluates whether theoretically defined facets ("subscales") of a
    questionnaire carry information beyond a general disposition when the scale
    also contains a wording (method) factor, for example from negatively keyed
    items. The package builds and compares one-factor, correlated-facet,
    bifactor and method-augmented bifactor models, and computes facet added-value
    indices (proportional reduction in mean squared error, value-added ratio,
    hierarchical omega) against a method-purified target true score that
    excludes wording variance. Naive indices that ignore the wording factor are
    reported alongside so the size of the misattribution is visible. Monte Carlo
    confidence intervals, a one-sided test of added value and between-group
    contrasts are provided. Methods build on Haberman (2008)
    <doi:10.3102/1076998607302636> and Feinberg and Wainer (2014)
    <doi:10.1111/emip.12035>.
